Subject: [PATCH 2/2] libtool: emit a SONAME from tcc's non-GNU-ld archive_cmds

Applies on top of 0001-libtool-tinycc-compiler-support.patch.

0001 backports upstream GNU libtool's `tcc*)` entries verbatim. One of
them -- the `linux*)` branch of `_LT_LINKER_SHLIBS` taken when `$LD` is
not GNU ld, which is exactly the branch reached under upstream's own
documented `./configure CC=tcc LD=tcc` -- sets

    archive_cmds='$CC -shared $pic_flag -o $lib $libobjs $deplibs $compiler_flags'

with no `-soname`. Every other spec in the same file that drives a
GNU-ld-style linker through `$CC` carries `${wl}-soname $wl$soname`
(the gnu-ld branch, sunos4, sysv5, the C++ tag, ...). The omission is
upstream's, not a property of tcc: tcc's `-Wl,` parser in `libtcc.c`
matches `soname=|install_name=` and its `link_option()` explicitly
supports the argument arriving in a following `-Wl,` group ("expecting
argument with next '-Wl,'"), so libtool's split spelling
`-Wl,-soname -Wl,libcrypto.so.57` is accepted as-is. tcc also stores it
into `TCCState.soname` and writes `DT_SONAME` in `tccelf.c`.

Consequence without this patch: a tcc-built `libcrypto.so.57.0.2` has no
`DT_SONAME`, so anything linking against it records the literal filename
it was handed rather than the versioned soname, and the resulting
libraries are not drop-in interchangeable with the gcc-built ones.

This does not address the second half of the divergence -- the tcc-built
libraries still export their whole symbol table rather than the set in
`crypto/crypto_portable.sym`. That needs `archive_expsym_cmds`, and both
spellings libtool has for it (`--version-script`, `--retain-symbols-file`)
are linker options tcc does not implement, so it is a tcc feature gap
rather than a libtool spec gap and is not fixable through this mechanism.
`archive_expsym_cmds` is left empty; `ltmain.sh` guards its use with
`test -n`, so the `-export-symbols`-bearing links fall back to
`archive_cmds` and pick the SONAME up too.

--- a/dep/libressl/configure
+++ b/dep/libressl/configure
@@ -10426,7 +10426,7 @@
       tcc*)
 	# Fabrice Bellard et al's Tiny C Compiler
 	ld_shlibs=yes
-	archive_cmds='$CC -shared $pic_flag -o $lib $libobjs $deplibs $compiler_flags'
+	archive_cmds='$CC -shared $pic_flag -o $lib $libobjs $deplibs $compiler_flags ${wl}-soname $wl$soname'
 	hardcode_libdir_flag_spec='${wl}-rpath ${wl}$libdir'
 	;;
       esac
--- a/dep/libressl/m4/libtool.m4
+++ b/dep/libressl/m4/libtool.m4
@@ -5357,7 +5357,7 @@
       tcc*)
 	# Fabrice Bellard et al's Tiny C Compiler
 	_LT_TAGVAR(ld_shlibs, $1)=yes
-	_LT_TAGVAR(archive_cmds, $1)='$CC -shared $pic_flag -o $lib $libobjs $deplibs $compiler_flags'
+	_LT_TAGVAR(archive_cmds, $1)='$CC -shared $pic_flag -o $lib $libobjs $deplibs $compiler_flags ${wl}-soname $wl$soname'
 	_LT_TAGVAR(hardcode_libdir_flag_spec, $1)='${wl}-rpath ${wl}$libdir'
 	;;
       esac
